<philosophy>

## Philosophy

Keep event processing simple: parse with `new Date()`, use native methods for comparisons, and rely on date-fns only for formatting and duration calculations. Timezones are left to the browser’s `Date` handling – by default, ISO strings like `2026-01-15T14:00:00Z` are parsed as UTC, and when you call `format()`, it will use the local time of the user’s computer. For display purposes this is usually correct.

```typescript
// Fast and reliable - modern Date constructor handles ISO 8601
const start = new Date("2026-01-15T14:00:00Z");
const end = new Date("2026-01-15T16:30:00Z");
```

</philosophy>

